Z||000000||RPM||05-13-2001||05:03 PM||||Hello, I don't own a Fiero, but I am interested in a single inlet, dual outlet Fiero muffler. I would like to use it to put dual outlets on my Miata. I have looked around a little and the Fiero muffler seems to be a good fit. What is the internal construction of the stock fiero muffler? I saw one at a junkyard but it had some honeycomb stuff coming out of it, like what comes out of the cat. I just want a cheap muffler, I did a search and Midas was recommended, If I go thru Midas what will the muffler come with? I need to rearrange the elbows to get the proper fit on the Miata, so just a case would be perfect, but unlikely. Thank you||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||05-13-2001||06:22 PM||||Most of us looking for performance get an aftermarket muffler for a camaro.  There are a lot of them available, in abundance for about 5 brands.  The only downside is that your small displacement motor might sound kind of funny with a muffler intended for a camaro...you will get all the flow you could ever need though.  FYI, if you take your car to a muffler shop that isn't a national chain, but rather a local shop with some actual knowledge other than bolting parts on, they will easily be able to accomodate any requests you will have of installing a dual outlet muffler.  Good luck, and for future reference, go to a miata forum and ask them.  Chances are a thousand people on the forum have done the same thing as you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||05-13-2001||10:39 PM||||SpinTech Mufflers  <A HREF="http://www.spintechmufflers.com" TARGET=_blank>www.spintechmufflers.com</A>  <BR>1-888-550-SPIN <P>331SC is 2.5" in and dual 2" out. 333SC same with dual 2.5" out. They have tons of others. Call them and tell them what you are doing.<P>Worth every penny.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RPM||05-14-2001||03:16 PM||||Most people on the Miata forum are using the camaro muffler, and they say it is loud. My usual custom exhaust shop owner also says a camaro muffler on a four cyl. is gonna talk. The reason I came to the fiero forum is because I am looking for a stock fiero muffler and I thought this would be the place to start. I'm not looking for a performance muffler, the stock 6-cyl will flow more than enough for a stock 4-cyl. I just want a cheap muffler that will have a decent tone. BTW I will be installing the whole system myself so I just need a muffler that will fit my needs. thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||05-15-2001||03:01 AM||||So if the Camaro and the Fiero muffler are basically interchangeable, and the Miata people use Camaro mufflers...lets do some deductive thinking.  We want a cheap muffler that won't be noisy, and will have the same design as the Camaro muffler...so, where should we turn to?  Why not just about any muffler shop in America...tell them you want a Fiero muffler, and they'll provide you with the cheapest, most muffling thing they offer.<P>Just remember, you get what you pay for.  And by the way, there aren't many muffler "upgrades" that don't produce more noise.||||reg||1
Z||000005||RPM||05-16-2001||11:15 AM||||Nashco: you are missing my point.||||reg||1
